# Ubuntu Touch: intentionally empty.
# The vendor init.qcom.usb.rc builds its own Android gadget (configs/b.1) on
# /config/usb_gadget/g1 and binds it to the UDC. That makes usb-moded's
# configurator fail ("mkdir configs/c.1: Device or resource busy"), so
# usb-moded never starts and the phone never shows up on USB (MTP/RNDIS/SSH).
# usb-moded owns the USB gadget on Ubuntu Touch.
